41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,- **Ryuji**: The bank statements show a third of renewals needed two reminders. Several members asked to spread payments. This confirms the cash flow is fragile.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"- **Minako**: @Ryuji, that payment fragility explains the hesitation. If the fee feels like a burden, people disengage. We need a structure that doesn't scare them off.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Minako, exactly. The winter social feedback shows people are anxious about the cost per visit. We need to remove that friction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"- **Shunichi**: @Ryuji, that payment fragility is a symptom, not the cause. The real issue is the uneven usage I found.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Ryuji, that payment fragility worries me. I hope the treasurer’s hours show the job isn’t too heavy for the next person.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, the hours confirm your fear. Chasing individual payments took six hours monthly, versus one for yearly. We must avoid that administrative burden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, that administrative burden is unacceptable. We cannot structure fees that force the next treasurer into that kind of labor.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Ryuji, that administrative burden is unacceptable. We cannot structure fees that force the next treasurer into that kind of labor.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the ledger confirms it. Seventy percent of costs are fixed, billed whether anyone attends. Activity-based charging won't solve the core problem.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Ryuji, six hours a month is too much. I can’t ask anyone to take that on. We need a simpler collection method.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, agreed. A flat annual fee minimizes that administrative load. We need a structure that is simple to collect and sustainable for the books.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, simplicity is vital, but we must ensure the fee doesn't alienate the eighteen members who never attend. We need a structure that feels fair to everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Minako, fairness means removing the fear of a full-year commitment. If the fee feels like a burden, people disengage.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, simplicity is fine, but it ignores the eighteen who never show. A flat fee forces them to subsidize the regulars. That’s the inequity I’m trying to fix.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
